---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
---

<Doc
	title="Privacy Policy | QuickStudy"
	description="Privacy policy for QuickStudy. No data is collected, and all AI processing runs on-device by default."
	eyebrow="QuickStudy"
	heading="Privacy Policy"
	intro="QuickStudy is built with privacy as a first principle. By default, no data ever leaves your device."
	footnote="Effective date: March 2026 · Last updated: March 2026"
>
	<section>
		<h2>No Data Collected</h2>
		<p>
			QuickStudy does not collect, transmit, store, or share any personal data. There are no user
			accounts, no sign-in requirements, and no analytics or tracking of any kind. QuickStudy's App
			Store privacy label reflects this: no data types are collected or linked to your identity.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>On-Device AI</h2>
		<p>
			By default, all AI features - including document summarisation and study card generation -
			run entirely on your device using Apple Foundation Models. Your documents, notes, and study
			content are never sent to any server or third-party AI service. No external AI provider has
			access to your content.
		</p>
		<p>
			QuickStudy also offers an optional external API feature that allows you to connect to
			third-party AI services. See the section below for important privacy information about this
			feature.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>External API Feature</h2>
		<p>
			QuickStudy includes an optional feature that allows you to use external AI APIs (such as
			those provided by third-party AI services). <strong>This feature is opt-in and disabled by
			default.</strong>
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				If you choose to enable and use this feature, any content you submit - including
				documents, notes, or prompts - will be transmitted to the external API provider you
				configure.
			</li>
			<li>
				Your data will be subject to that provider's own privacy policy, terms of service, and
				data retention practices.
			</li>
			<li>
				The QuickStudy developer has no control over how third-party API providers collect,
				process, store, or share your data.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Before using the external API feature, you are encouraged to review the privacy policy of the
			API provider you intend to use. You are responsible for ensuring that your use of a
			third-party API complies with any applicable laws and the provider's terms of service.
		</p>
		<p>
			You can disable the external API feature at any time in the app's settings, which will revert
			all AI processing to on-device Apple Foundation Models.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Local Storage & Data Retention</h2>
		<p>
			QuickStudy stores your content locally using AppStorage and UserDefaults - standard iOS
			storage mechanisms. Nothing is synced to external servers. Because no data is collected by
			the app, there is no server-side retention period.
		</p>
		<p>
			All locally stored content (your documents, scan history, and study cards) is retained on
			your device until you delete it within the app or uninstall QuickStudy. Uninstalling the app
			permanently removes all associated local data.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>App Permissions</h2>
		<p>QuickStudy may request the following iOS permissions:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Camera</strong> - used only to scan physical documents. Images are processed
				on-device and are never uploaded.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Photo Library / Files</strong> - used only when you choose to import a document or
				PDF. Imported content is processed on-device and never leaves your device.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Permissions are requested only when you initiate the relevant action. You can revoke
			permissions at any time in iOS Settings.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>No Third-Party SDKs</h2>
		<p>
			QuickStudy contains no third-party analytics, advertising, crash reporting, or tracking
			frameworks. There are no external dependencies that could introduce data collection or
			sharing by a third party.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Deleting Your Data</h2>
		<p>
			Because all data is stored locally on your device, you are always in full control of it. You
			can delete individual documents or study sets within the app at any time. To remove all data
			associated with QuickStudy, uninstall the app from your device. This permanently deletes all
			locally stored content.
		</p>
		<p>
			There is no account to close and no server-side data to request deletion of - none exists.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Your Rights</h2>
		<p>
			Depending on where you live, you may have rights regarding your personal data under
			applicable law (including the EU General Data Protection Regulation, UK GDPR, and California
			Consumer Privacy Act). Because QuickStudy does not collect, process, or store any personal
			data on external systems, there is no personal data held by the developer to access, correct,
			export, or erase.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you have any questions or wish to exercise any rights, you can contact the developer
			directly at <a href="mailto:jaidenhenleydev@gmail.com">jaidenhenleydev@gmail.com</a>.
		</p>
		<p><strong>Data controller:</strong> Jaiden Henley - jaidenhenleydev@gmail.com</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
		<p>
			QuickStudy is not directed at children under the age of 13 (or under 16 in applicable EU
			member states). The app does not knowingly collect any personal information from children.
			Because no data is collected from any user, no data is collected from minors.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Apple's Role</h2>
		<p>
			QuickStudy is distributed through the Apple App Store. Apple may collect certain device and
			transaction information as part of operating the App Store and iOS platform. This collection
			is governed by <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>, not this policy. The QuickStudy developer has no
			access to any data Apple collects.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you use iCloud Backup, iOS will include your locally stored QuickStudy data in that
			backup. This is managed entirely by Apple and iOS - the developer has no access to backed-up
			content.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
		<p>
			If this policy is updated, the revised version will be posted at this URL with an updated
			date. Continued use of the app after any change constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			For any questions about this privacy policy, contact:
			<a href="mailto:jaidenhenleydev@gmail.com">jaidenhenleydev@gmail.com</a>
		</p>
	</section>
</Doc>
